@@ -96,11 +96,17 @@ variables. Unlike the path, where multiple parts are separated by ``/``, the
 domain is always matched as a single part.
 
 If a duplicate rule is added to a map, a :exc:`.DuplicateRuleError` will be
-raised. Rules are compared based on their path, subdomain or host, and websocket
-mode. Variable parts are not equal if they use different converters, although
-this heuristic may not be perfect depending on what the different converters can
+raised. Rules are compared based on their path, subdomain or host, websocket
+mode, and methods. Rules are only duplicates if they share at least one method;
+a rule with no ``methods`` matches every method, so it overlaps any other rule.
+Variable parts are not equal if they use different converters, although this
+heuristic may not be perfect depending on what the different converters can
 actually match.
 
+``merge_slashes`` is accounted for, because it affects how the path is split
+into parts. ``strict_slashes`` does not affect the comparison, as it only
+controls how a branch URL that is missing its trailing slash is handled.
+
 
 Rule Priority
